From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Komh <mail@guojing.io>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:24:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] extra-data: prefetch downloads in parallel

A transaction downloads extra-data one operation at a time over a single
connection. Once the transaction is ready, start downloading every
operation's extra-data in a thread pool (4 at a time, at most 4 per
host) while the operations still run in order; pulling extra-data then
waits for the prefetched file instead of downloading it again. Failures
fall back to the original download path.

Downloads go to <user dir>/extra-data/<sha256>/<name>.part, are verified
and renamed into place, and the directory gets a .flatpak-prefetch
marker: a verified file left over by an interrupted run is reused, and
everything is removed once the operation is done. SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP
make flatpak _exit() from the signal handler, so the handler removes
the prefetched files itself, with async-signal-safe calls only. Files
the user put there (no marker) are never touched.

Tunable with `flatpak config --set extra-data-parallel N` or
FLATPAK_EXTRA_DATA_PARALLEL=N; 1 restores the serial behaviour.
